ck's cells must be covered by rectangles that lie entirely within that block. They cannot be covered by rectangles from other blocks because blocks are disjoint. So they must cover all cells within each block, except the uncovered cell. But they only cover the row and column strips, leaving the bottom-right subblock uncovered. That's a huge oversight. However, maybe they intend that the bottom-right subblock is covered by the rectangle R_{a,b} for some off-diagonal block? No, that would be a different block. Off-diagonal blocks are B_{a,b} for a≠b, which are separate. The bottom-right subblock of diagonal block B_{a,a} is still part of B_{a,a}. So they need to cover it. In the interior diagonal blocks (a≥4),",
